## Original Content
🇰🇪 Au Kenya, un jeune créateur de mode mise sur le tissage manuel pour se démarquer. Il fabrique des tissus et des vêtements à la main, faisant revivre un savoir-faire traditionnel menacé par l’industrialisation.

## Summary
A young fashion designer in Kenya is reviving traditional manual weaving to stand out in the industry. He handcrafts fabrics and clothing, preserving an artisanal skill that is threatened by industrialization. This effort highlights the role of cultural heritage in modern fashion.

## Key Points
- Young fashion designer in Kenya relies on manual weaving for differentiation.
- Traditional textiles and garments are being crafted by hand.
- Industrialization poses a threat to traditional weaving skills.
- The article emphasizes preserving cultural craftsmanship in contemporary contexts.


